.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt XFT_FUZZER 3
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft_new_fuzzer ,
.Nm xft_fuzzer_add_rand ,
.Nm xft_fuzz_get_rand ,
.Nm xft_fuzz_get_rand_u ,
.Nm xft_fuzz_get_rand_d ,
.Nm xft_fuzzer_destroy
.Nd random input pool for fuzz targets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In fuzzer.h
.Fd #define XFT_FUZZ_MIN_INIT 50000
.Fd #define XFT_FUZZ_MAX_INIT 300000
.Ft t_fuzzer
.Fn xft_new_fuzzer "t_arena arena"
.Ft t_result
.Fn xft_fuzzer_add_rand "t_fuzzer *fuzz"
.Ft t_buffer *
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand "t_fuzzer *fuzz"
.Ft t_u64a
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand_u "t_fuzzer *fuzz"
.Ft t_f64
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand_d "t_fuzzer *fuzz"
.Ft void
.Fn xft_fuzzer_destroy "t_fuzzer *f"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A fuzzer is a pool of randomly sized buffers carved from an arena plus a
xoshiro256** generator used to pick buffers and produce random numbers.
.In fuzzer.h
is not included by
.In xft.h .
.Ss Types
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Vt t_fuzzer
.Fa xo ,
the
.Vt t_xoshiro
state;
.Fa arena ,
which owns all memory;
.Fa buffers
and
.Fa buf_n ,
the pool and its length;
.Fa lastgen ,
the last value handed out.
.It Vt t_lastgen
.Fa type ,
a
.Vt t_lastgentype
.Pq Dv BUFFER , UNSIGNED , DOUBLE ,
and
.Fa as ,
a
.Vt t_lastgenval
with members
.Fa u ,
.Fa d
and
.Fa b .
Only the member matching the generator that set it is meaningful.
.El
.Ss Functions
.Fn xft_new_fuzzer
returns a fuzzer that takes ownership of
.Fa arena ,
with an empty pool.
The generator is seeded by
.Fn xft_xoshiro_init ,
which mixes in a stack address and
.Fn xft_get_nanos ,
so runs are not reproducible.
.Fa lastgen
is left uninitialized.
.Pp
.Fn xft_fuzzer_add_rand
fills the pool.
It picks a count
.Fa n
in
.Bq Dv XFT_FUZZ_MIN_INIT , Dv XFT_FUZZ_MIN_INIT No + Dv XFT_FUZZ_MAX_INIT No \- 1 ,
allocates an array of
.Fa n
.Vt t_buffer
from the arena, sets
.Fa buf_n
to
.Fa n ,
and allocates each buffer from the arena with a random size from 1 to 1024
bytes and a random alignment of 1, 4, 16 or 64.
The buffer contents are not written; they hold whatever the arena returns,
which for fresh arena pages is all zero bytes.
.Pp
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand
returns a uniformly chosen buffer from the pool.
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand_u
returns 64 random bits.
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand_d
returns 64 random bits reinterpreted as a
.Vt t_f64 ,
so it can be any value including NaN, infinities and subnormals.
Each records its result in
.Fa fuzz Ns .lastgen .
.Pp
.Fn xft_fuzzer_destroy
destroys the arena, releasing the pool and every buffer.
.Ss Fuzz targets
The fuzz targets live in
.Pa fuzz/
and are built with
.Fl Dfuzz ,
which requires
.Fl Dsanitize
and
.Fl Duse-libc .
They are
.Cm fuzz_mem
.Pq Pa fuzz/mem_fuzz.c ,
.Cm fuzz_vec
.Pq Pa fuzz/vec_fuzz.c
and
.Cm fuzz_map
.Pq Pa fuzz/map_fuzz.c ,
run by the
.Cm fuzz
build step.
They link the main library, which those options make sanitized and
hosted.
.Pp
Each target creates a fuzzer over
.Fn xft_new_arena ,
fills it once, runs
.Fa buf_n
\(mu 2 cases comparing xft routines against libc or checking container
invariants with
.Xr xft_hint 3 ,
then destroys the fuzzer and exits with status 0.
A failed check exits with status 1.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xft_new_fuzzer
returns the fuzzer by value.
.Fn xft_fuzzer_add_rand
returns
.Dv OK
on success and
.Dv KO
if an arena allocation fails.
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand
returns a pointer into the pool, valid until
.Fn xft_fuzzer_destroy .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build and run the fuzz targets:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zig build -Duse-libc -Dsanitize -Dfuzz fuzz
.Ed
.Pp
A target, after
.Pa fuzz/mem_fuzz.c :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>
#include <fuzzer.h>

void	xft_main(const t_any *__restrict__ const sp)
{
	t_fuzzer	fz;
	t_buffer	*b;
	t_size		i;

	(void)sp;
	fz = xft_new_fuzzer(xft_new_arena());
	xft_pin_invariant(fz.arena.current != nullptr);
	xft_pin_invariant(xft_fuzzer_add_rand(&fz));
	i = 0;
	while (i++ < fz.buf_n * 2)
	{
		b = xft_fuzz_get_rand(&fz);
		xft_pin_invariant(xft_memchr(b->mem, b->mem[0], b->size)
			== b->mem);
	}
	xft_fuzzer_destroy(&fz);
	xft_exit(0);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xft_hint 3 ,
.Xr xft_mem 3 ,
.Xr xft_rng 3 ,
.Xr xft 7
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand
divides by
.Fa buf_n ;
call
.Fn xft_fuzzer_add_rand
first.
.Pp
.Fn xft_fuzzer_add_rand
is only correct when called once.
A second call allocates a fresh array, leaves its first
.Fa buf_n
entries uninitialized and, if the new count is smaller, shrinks the pool
without initializing anything.
If a buffer allocation fails, the arena is rewound but
.Fa buffers
and
.Fa buf_n
still describe the rewound memory.
.Pp
.Fn xft_fuzz_get_rand_d
records
.Dv UNSIGNED ,
not
.Dv DOUBLE ,
in
.Fa lastgen Ns .type .
